# The work morning: yesterday's Slack mentions, Jira issues and GitHub
# notifications, triaged into a digest you review; the suggested replies
# posted only once you approve them. The tool names are those of the
# stand-ins harness's tests use: put your servers' own (harness mcp list).
workflow morning
about Weekday mornings: what came in from Slack, Jira and GitHub, triaged into a digest you review; the suggested replies posted once you approve them.
start owner, schedule:morning-at
limits steps 20, days 1

step slack
tool slack/search_messages {"query": "to:me after:yesterday"}
retry 2 wait 5m

step jira
tool jira/search_issues {"jql": "assignee = currentUser() AND updated >= -1d ORDER BY priority DESC"}
retry 2 wait 5m

step github
tool github/list_notifications {"participating": true}
retry 2 wait 5m

step triage
answer json
tools none
do:
  Triage what came in since yesterday (the data below) into the owner's
  morning digest: first what needs them today, with who asked and where;
  then the rest, a line each. Suggest a reply only where a short one moves
  things on, in the owner's voice, and never promise a time they didn't give.
  Answer only JSON:
  {"digest": "...",
   "replies": [{"where": "slack", "channel": "#...", "thread_ts": "...", "text": "..."},
               {"where": "github", "owner": "...", "repo": "...", "issue": 1, "text": "..."}],
   "replies_text": "one line a reply: where, then the text"}
  Slack mentions: {slack}
  Jira issues: {jira}
  GitHub notifications: {github}

step review
review {triage.digest}

step tell
say {review}

step ask
approve:
  Post these replies?
  {triage.replies_text}
on deny goto done

step post
tools slack/post_message, github/add_issue_comment
do:
  Post each of these replies once, exactly as written, where it says:
  Slack replies with slack/post_message (channel, thread_ts, text);
  GitHub replies with github/add_issue_comment (owner, repo, issue_number,
  body). Post nothing else. Answer with one line a reply: where it went.
  The replies: {triage.replies}

step posted
say:
  Replies posted:
  {post}

step done
end
